window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>The line between good and evil is seldom pure and never simple ...</p> <p>I used to think the truth was as clear and pure as my heart. Now, nothing is certain. Not the love I feel for two men—one reborn in darkness, the other clawing his way back to me. And certainly not the prophesy telling me that I'm destined to become the Fourth Horseman.</p> <p>The Order has given me my mission: fulfill my destiny by destroying Lucifer's unborn child and the girl carrying it. But destiny has never felt so wrong. Every instinct is screaming that this child isn't the monster they say it is. That it's something else entirely—something terrifyingly familiar.</p> <p>What if the real danger has been right in front of my eyes all this time?</p> <p>The deeper I dig, the more the world twists around me. Illusions masquerade as truth and all of it tastes like a carefully woven lie. I still don't know what to do, who to love, or which side to trust.</p> <p>All I know is that one choice will break me.</p> <p>The other one might doom us all.</p> <p>Either way, I'm going to lose everything.</p> <p><i>Illusory </i>is the highly anticipated eight book in the Marked Saga, a fast-paced paranormal fantasy romance series full of heart-pounding steam, supernatural adventure, and jaw-dropping twists that will keep you on the edge of your seat until the very last moment. Please note, this is a massive 180K-word double-feature book that ends on a cliff-hanger.</p> <p>Listener discretion: This book contains graphic language and sexual content and is not suitable for listeners under 17.</p>"; 
